.TH VSCODE-SWITCH-TAB 1 "2026-07-29" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vscode-switch-tab \- request a VS Code integrated-terminal tab switch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vscode-switch-tab
.RI [ next | previous ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vscode-switch-tab
asks VS Code, through its pluggable command-execution bridge (see
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_BACKEND
below), to switch the focused integrated-terminal tab. Consumers such as
tmux and Neovim call this when the focused application cannot handle the
key itself and there is nothing left to switch locally. With a single
terminal open the request is a silent no-op, matching how every other tab
layer behaves at its own edge.
.PP
When the local
.B cgraf.termnav
adapter advertises a per-window socket, the command uses it to keep
simultaneous VS Code windows isolated. Otherwise it retains the MCP backend as
a rollout fallback. It fails silently (non-zero exit, no output) if the
selected bridge is unreachable.
.PP
Adapter sockets are activation-scoped. Reloading the editor window or its
extension host requires relaunching existing terminal or tmux clients so they
receive the new socket path; stale clients fail closed.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B next
Switch to the next terminal tab. This is the default.
.TP
.B previous
Switch to the previous terminal tab.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_BACKEND
Selects the command-execution backend. When unset, paired nonempty
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_SOCKET
and
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_TOKEN
selects
.BR socket ;
otherwise the fallback is
.BR mcp .
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_SOCKET
Owner-only Unix socket published into terminals by the local adapter.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_TOKEN
Random per-window capability required by the socket backend.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_CURL
HTTP client used by the socket backend. Defaults to
.BR curl .
.TP
.B VSCODE_MCP_PORT
Overrides the optional MCP backend's target port. Defaults to
.BR 9876 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command was executed.
.TP
.B 1
The bridge was unreachable or the command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termnav-switch-tab (1),
.BR wezterm-switch-tab (1)
